@page "/"

<PageTitle>Home</PageTitle>

<!-- Hero: full width, two columns - right column reserved for a future
     graphic. First attempt (bankroll-trajectories.png) shelved for now -
     couldn't get the layout to close the gap between it and the page
     content below despite confirmed-working style changes; revisit later
     rather than keep tuning blind. Image file left in wwwroot/images. -->
<MudGrid Class="mb-8">
    <MudItem xs="12" md="8">
        <MudText Typo="Typo.h4" GutterBottom="true">Welcome to Blackjack Streak Simulator!</MudText>
        <MudText Typo="Typo.h6" Class="mb-4">Does a "crazy" betting system actually change your odds? Let's find out.</MudText>
        <MudText Class="mb-4">
            Simulate thousands of blackjack sessions using the Paroli betting system and see
            what actually happens.
        </MudText>
        <MudStack Row="true" Spacing="4">
            <MudButton Variant="Variant.Filled" Color="Color.Primary" Href="/simconfig">Configure a Simulation</MudButton>
            <MudButton Variant="Variant.Outlined" Color="Color.Primary" Href="/batchsim">Run a Batch Simulation</MudButton>
            <MudButton Variant="Variant.Outlined" Color="Color.Primary" Href="/stepthrough">Step Through a Game</MudButton>
        </MudStack>
    </MudItem>
    <MudItem xs="12" md="4">
        <!-- Reserved for a hero graphic - shelved for now, see comment above. -->
    </MudItem>
</MudGrid>

<!-- Narrower reading width for pure prose - reads better around 800-950px
     than stretched across the full page. The expanders below get their
     own wider container instead of sharing this one, since their cards
     need more room than prose does. -->
<div style="max-width: 900px;">
    <MudText Typo="Typo.h5" Color="Color.Primary" Class="section-header" GutterBottom="true">Why I built this</MudText>
    <MudText Class="mb-8">
        Years ago, a friend and I went to Vegas and played blackjack together. He used a
        betting system that looked crazy to me at the time - but he walked away from that
        trip a winner, and I've wondered ever since whether that was the system, or just
        luck.
        <br /><br />
        It turns out the system has a name - <b>Paroli</b> - and mathematicians have
        already worked out its odds in exhaustive detail. I'm not a mathematician, but I
        am a software developer. So instead of doing the math myself, I built something
        that plays it out: thousands of simulated hands, with the results laid out for
        you to explore.
    </MudText>
</div>

<!-- Wider than the prose column above - the cards inside these panels felt
     cramped at 900px. Not full page width, just enough room to breathe. -->
<div style="max-width: 1150px;">
    <MudExpansionPanels Class="mb-8">
        <MudExpansionPanel>
            <TitleContent>
                <MudText Typo="Typo.h6" Color="Color.Primary" Class="section-header">How Paroli betting works</MudText>
            </TitleContent>
            <ChildContent>
                <MudGrid Class="mb-4">
                    <MudItem xs="12" sm="4">
                        <MudCard>
                            <MudCardContent>
                                <MudText Typo="Typo.subtitle1"><b>Paroli</b></MudText>
                                <MudText Typo="Typo.body2" Class="mb-2">Win, double, double, reset</MudText>
                                <MudText Typo="Typo.h6">$10 &rarr; $20 &rarr; $40 &rarr; reset</MudText>
                            </MudCardContent>
                        </MudCard>
                    </MudItem>
                    <MudItem xs="12" sm="4">
                        <MudCard>
                            <MudCardContent>
                                <MudText Typo="Typo.subtitle1"><b>Flat Betting</b></MudText>
                                <MudText Typo="Typo.body2" Class="mb-2">The same bet every hand</MudText>
                                <MudText Typo="Typo.h6">$10 &rarr; $10 &rarr; $10 &rarr; $10</MudText>
                            </MudCardContent>
                        </MudCard>
                    </MudItem>
                    <MudItem xs="12" sm="4">
                        <MudCard>
                            <MudCardContent>
                                <MudText Typo="Typo.subtitle1"><b>Standard Strategy</b></MudText>
                                <MudText Typo="Typo.body2">For both Paroli and Flat betting, every player uses the same well-established strategy - only bet sizing changes.</MudText>
                            </MudCardContent>
                        </MudCard>
                    </MudItem>
                </MudGrid>
                <MudText>
                    Lose at any point during a Paroli streak, and you're straight back to your $10 base bet.
                    <b>Flat betting</b> - what most players actually do - just keeps the same bet every hand,
                    win or lose. This app lets you run both side by side.
                    <br /><br />
                    Betting is only half the picture, though. Every player at the table - including the one
                    being tracked - always plays the same well-established
                    <MudLink Href="basic-strategy.html" Target="_blank">standard strategy</MudLink> for how to
                    play each hand. Nobody's making judgment calls; only the bet sizing changes.
                </MudText>
            </ChildContent>
        </MudExpansionPanel>
        <MudExpansionPanel>
            <TitleContent>
                <MudText Typo="Typo.h6" Color="Color.Primary" Class="section-header">What you can do here</MudText>
            </TitleContent>
            <ChildContent>
                <MudText>
                    In <b>Simulation Configuration</b>, you can set your starting bankroll, base bet, goal,
                    and streak length, and choose between Paroli-style streak betting or flat betting.
                    <br /><br />
                    In <b>Step-Through Simulation</b>, you can play a single simulated game one hand at a
                    time. There's no real strategic reason to watch it live - every seat plays fixed basic
                    strategy, nobody's making decisions - it's mostly here to show off Blazor's interactive
                    rendering.
                    <br /><br />
                    In <b>Batch Simulation</b>, you can run however many simulated attempts you like - 1,000
                    is a good starting point - and see what happened: how often the goal got hit, how often
                    the bankroll went <i>bankrupt</i>, and how rough the ride was along the way.
                    <br /><br />
                    In <b>Batch History</b>, you can look back at every batch you've run, compare
                    configurations side by side, and dig into the details - streak lengths, drawdowns, and
                    lowest-bankroll buckets - for any past batch.
                </MudText>
            </ChildContent>
        </MudExpansionPanel>
    </MudExpansionPanels>
</div>

<div style="max-width: 900px;">
    <MudText Typo="Typo.h5" Color="Color.Primary" Class="section-header" GutterBottom="true">About this project</MudText>
    <MudText Class="mb-4">
        This application is both a working simulation and a demonstration of my software
        development skills. The <MudLink Href="/techstack">Technology Stack</MudLink> page
        describes the architecture and technologies used throughout.
        <br /><br />
        I didn't type most of the code in this repository myself - but I made every design
        decision, reviewed every line, and directed the build end-to-end using <b>Claude
        Code</b> as my implementation partner. Knowing how to effectively direct, evaluate, and
        take ownership of AI-generated code is itself a real engineering skill, and this project
        is a demonstration of exactly that.
        <br /><br />
        This project was started in early August 2026 and completed mid-September 2026.
    </MudText>
    <MudButton Variant="Variant.Outlined" Color="Color.Primary" Href="/techstack" Class="mb-8">View Technology Stack</MudButton>
</div>
